<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Syria</h1><p class="st-meta">1946 CE – present · capital Damascus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Syrian republic, independent of France in 1946, a seat of Arab nationalism, ruled for half a century by the Assads and shattered by civil war.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/arab-kingdom-of-syria">Arab Kingdom of Syria</a> fell to French arms in 1920, nationalists fought the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-mandate-for-syria-and-the-lebanon">mandate</a> through the great revolt of 1925-1927 and pressed on through treaties and elections until the last French troops left in April 1946.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Coups shook the young republic until the Ba'ath Party seized power in 1963; Hafez al-Assad took control in 1970 and built a security state around his family and the army. Syria lost the Golan Heights in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/six-day-war">Six-Day War</a>, fought again in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yom-kippur-war">Yom Kippur War</a> of 1973, and garrisoned Lebanon from 1976 to 2005.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>The uprising of 2011 against Bashar al-Assad became a civil war that killed hundreds of thousands, displaced half the population and drew in outside powers; the Assad government fell in December 2024, leaving Syria's reconstruction and unity an open question.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1946 CE – present"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:98.43%;width:1.57%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1946 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Damascus</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Presidents of Syria</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (majority), Alawite, Christian and Druze minorities</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Syrian Arab Republic, Republic of Syria</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1986&amp;focus=syria" aria-label="Syria on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5607 962 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Syria lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5927 1218L5905 1205"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5905 1205h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5927 1218h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5927 1218h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1986&amp;focus=syria">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
